{
  "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
  "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As a condition of receiving a residential building permit, petitioner George Sheetz was required by the County of El Dorado to pay a $23,420 traffc impact fee."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He later sought relief in state court, claiming that conditioning the building permit on the payment of a traffc impact fee constituted an unlawful \u201cexac- tion\u201d of money in violation of the Takings Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The courts below ruled against Sheetz based on their view that Nollan and Dolan apply only to permit conditions imposed on an ad hoc basis by administrators, not to a fee like this one imposed on a class of property owners by Board-enacted legislation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Erica L. Ross argued the cause for the United States as amicus curiae urging affrmance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0000-0006",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The County's predetermined fee schedule, Sheetz argued, failed to meet that requirement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0000-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We granted certiorari to resolve the split."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In sum, there is no basis for affording property rights less protection in the hands of legislators than administrators. The Takings Clause applies equally to both\u2014which means that it prohibits legislatures and agencies alike from imposing unconstitutional conditions on land-use permits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "County",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The County no longer contends otherwise. In fact, at oral argument, the parties expressed \u201cradical agreement\u201d that conditions on building permits are not exempt from scrutiny"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b261065d40e4cb99c40a8b5f0fdee452ea6258f9ac94414fa81aa58e85992ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b261065d40e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "a compensable taking if imposed outside the permitting context."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
